/-!
# Formal functions in degree zero; relative `Proj` of an algebra generated in degree one

Let `f : Y ⟶ Z` be a proper morphism of Noetherian schemes, `ℱ` a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module and
`z : Z` a point, with local ring `A = 𝒪_{Z,z}` and maximal ideal `𝔪 = 𝔪_z`. Write
`Y_k = Y ×_Z Spec (A/𝔪ᵏ)` for the infinitesimal neighbourhoods of the fibre over `z` and
`ℱ_k = i_k^* ℱ` for the pull-back of `ℱ` to `Y_k`. A section of `ℱ` over `f⁻¹ U`, for `U` an
open neighbourhood of `z`, restricts to a section of `ℱ_k` over all of `Y_k`; these
restrictions assemble into the natural map

`((f_* ℱ)_z)^∧ ⟶ lim_k H⁰(Y_k, ℱ_k)`

out of the `𝔪`-adic completion, and the theorem on formal functions in degree zero says that it
is an isomorphism. For `ℱ = 𝒪_Y` the same restrictions give the isomorphism
`((f_* 𝒪_Y)_z)^∧ ≅ lim_k Γ(Y_k, 𝒪_{Y_k})` of the completed algebra with the limit of the
rings of functions on the thickenings, and the isomorphism for `ℱ` is compatible with the
actions of the two sides: on each `Y_k` the restriction of `a • s` is the restriction of `a`
acting on the restriction of `s`.

Second, let `Y` be a Noetherian scheme and `R = ⨁_{m ≥ 0} R_m` a quasi-coherent graded
`𝒪_Y`-algebra with `R_0 = 𝒪_Y`, every `R_m` coherent, `R` a sheaf of integral domains, and `R`
generated by `R_1`, and let `g : Z = Proj_Y R ⟶ Y` be its relative `Proj`. Then `g` is
projective, the twisting sheaf `𝒪_Z(1)` is invertible and `g`-ample, and the canonical map
`R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪_Z(m)` is an isomorphism for all `m ≫ 0`. Multiplication gives a surjection
`Sym R_1 ⟶ R`, so `Proj_Y R` is a closed subscheme of the projective bundle `𝐏(R_1)`. Over an
affine open `W` of `Y`, the part of `Z` over `W` is the quasi-compact `Proj Γ(W, R)`, covered by
the affine degree-one standard opens, so `𝒪(1)` is ample there; and the comparison of degree-`m`
elements with global sections of `𝒪(m)` is bijective for `m ≫ 0` (Stacks 0AG7), which glues
over a finite affine cover of `Y`.

## Main results

* `MMP.exists_adicCompletion_pushforward_stalk_linearEquiv_towerLimit`: the theorem on formal
  functions in degree zero, with its algebra compatibility.
* `MMP.Foundations.ConeAlgebra.isProjective_and_isIso_pieceToPushforwardTwist`: the relative
  `Proj` of a degree-one generated algebra is projective, `𝒪(1)` is relatively ample, and
  `R_m ≅ g_* 𝒪(m)` for `m ≫ 0`.

## Implementation notes

The limit is `Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit`, the submodule of compatible families in
the product. For the structure sheaf the tower is `Stacks.FormalFunctions.infinitesimalFunctions`
and the comparison is `Stacks.FormalFunctions.canonicalStalkComparison`. For `ℱ` the transition
maps `H⁰(Y_n, ℱ_n) ⟶ H⁰(Y_m, ℱ_m)` enter as an arbitrary family of `A`-linear maps whose
underlying functions are the restrictions along `t : Y_m ⟶ Y_n` (the unit `ℱ_n ⟶ t_* t^* ℱ_n`
followed by `t^* ℱ_n ≅ ℱ_m`); this pins them uniquely. The completion `((f_* 𝒪_Y)_z)^∧` is
taken `𝔪`-adically over `A`, where Mathlib carries no ring structure on it and no action of it
on `((f_* ℱ)_z)^∧`. The compatibility of the actions is therefore stated on the classes of germs,
which are dense in the completions; the action of the completed algebra is the continuous
extension of that one.

For the relative `Proj`, the graded algebra is a relative `Proj` situation
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation` (a commutative, quasi-coherent, nonnegatively graded
`𝒪_Y`-algebra) satisfying Fulton's conditions `MMP.Intersection.Scheme.IsConeAlgebra`
(`R_0 = 𝒪_Y`, `R_1` coherent, locally generated by `R_1`). Its relative `Proj` is
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProj`, with projection
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProjToBase` and twisting sheaves
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.twistSheaf`. "Sheaf of integral domains" is read as: the ring
`⨁_m R_m(U)` of sections over every nonempty open `U` is a domain. Projectivity is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective` (Stacks Tag 01W8: a closed immersion over `Y` into the
projective bundle of a quasi-coherent module of finite type). Relative ampleness is
`Stacks.RelativeAmple.IsRelativelyAmple` (Stacks Tag 01VH: ample over the preimage of every
affine open of `Y`).

The canonical map `R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪_Z(m)` is characterised by its values. Over an affine open `W` of
`Y`, the part of `Z` lying over `W` is the chart `Proj Γ(W, R)`, where `𝒪_Z(m)` restricts to the
twisting sheaf `𝒪(m)` (`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.twistSheafChartIso`). A section
`a ∈ R_m(W)` is sent to the section of `𝒪(m)` that the homogeneous element `a` defines
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection`). The charts cover `Z`, so this
determines the map.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OD)
* [EGA III, 4.1.5]
* [EGA II, 3.3, 4.5, 4.6]
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NS)
-/

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite Stacks.FormalFunctions
  Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration

namespace MMP

/-- Restricting a section of `ℱ` over `f ⁻¹ U` to the `n`-th infinitesimal neighbourhood of the
fibre over `y` is semilinear along `Stacks.FormalFunctions.infinitesimalRestrict`. -/
private theorem infinitesimalRestrict_smul_res {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (F : X.Modules)
    (y : Y) (n : ℕ) (U : Y.Opens) (hy : y ∈ U) (a : Γ(X, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) (s : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) :
    (infinitesimalModule f F y n).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (top_le_preimage_infinitesimalι f y n U hy)).op
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (infinitesimalι f y n)).unit.app F).app
          (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (a • s)) =
      infinitesimalRestrict f y n U hy a •
        (infinitesimalModule f F y n).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (top_le_preimage_infinitesimalι f y n U hy)).op
          (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (infinitesimalι f y n)).unit.app F).app
            (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) s) := by
  rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul]
  erw [Scheme.Modules.map_smul]
  congr 1

/-- **The theorem on formal functions in degree zero, with the action of the completed algebra**
[Stacks, Tag 02OD]. Let `f : Y ⟶ Z` be proper between Noetherian schemes, `ℱ` coherent on `Y`
and `z : Z`. Then the canonical comparison `((f_* 𝒪_Y)_z)^∧ ⟶ lim_k Γ(Y_k, 𝒪_{Y_k})` is
bijective, and there is an `𝒪_{Z,z}`-linear isomorphism `Φ` from the `𝔪_z`-adic completion of
`(f_* ℱ)_z` to the limit of the tower `H⁰(Y_k, ℱ_k)` (along the restriction maps `φ`) whose
`k`-th component sends the class of the germ of a section `s` over `f⁻¹ U` to the restriction of
`s` to `Y_k = Stacks.FormalFunctions.infinitesimalNeighbourhood f z k`. It is compatible with
the actions: for a function `a` on `f⁻¹ U`, the `k`-th component of `Φ` on the germ of `a • s`
is the restriction of `a` to `Y_k` acting on the `k`-th component of `Φ` on the germ of `s`. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_foundation_fa17_formal_functions_ring_module"]
public theorem exists_adicCompletion_pushforward_stalk_linearEquiv_towerLimit
    {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ Z) [IsNoetherian Y] [IsNoetherian Z] [IsProper f]
    (F : Y.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] (z : Z) :
    letI H : ℕ → Type u := fun k => Γ(infinitesimalModule f F z k, ⊤)
    letI : ∀ k, Module (Z.presheaf.stalk z) (H k) := fun k =>
      Module.compHom _ (infinitesimalBaseRingHom f z k)
    letI res : ∀ (k : ℕ) (U : Z.Opens), z ∈ U → Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ U) → H k := fun k U hz s =>
      (infinitesimalModule f F z k).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (top_le_preimage_infinitesimalι f z k U hz)).op
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (infinitesimalι f z k)).unit.app F).app
          (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) s)
    ∀ (φ : ∀ m n, m ≤ n → H n →ₗ[Z.presheaf.stalk z] H m),
      (∀ m n (h : m ≤ n) (x : H n), φ m n h x =
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp (infinitesimalTransition f z h)
              (infinitesimalι f z n)).hom.app F ≫
            (Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr (infinitesimalTransition_ι f z h)).hom.app F).app ⊤
          ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (infinitesimalTransition f z h)).obj
              (infinitesimalModule f F z n) |>.presheaf.map
            (homOfLE (top_le_preimage_top (infinitesimalTransition f z h))).op
            (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction
              (infinitesimalTransition f z h)).unit.app (infinitesimalModule f F z n)).app ⊤ x))) →
      Function.Bijective (canonicalStalkComparison f z) ∧
      ∃ Φ : AdicCompletion (stalkMaximalIdeal z)
          (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).presheaf.stalk z) ≃ₗ[Z.presheaf.stalk z]
            towerLimit H φ,
        (∀ k (U : Z.Opens) (hz : z ∈ U) (s : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)),
          towerLimit.proj k (Φ (AdicCompletion.of _ _
            (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).presheaf.germ U z hz s))) = res k U hz s) ∧
        (∀ k (U : Z.Opens) (hz : z ∈ U) (a : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) (s : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)),
          towerLimit.proj k (Φ (AdicCompletion.of _ _
            (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).presheaf.germ U z hz (a • s)))) =
            infinitesimalRestrict f z k U hz a •
              towerLimit.proj k (Φ (AdicCompletion.of _ _
                (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).presheaf.germ U z hz s)))) := by
  intro φ hφ
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian Z := IsNoetherian.toIsLocallyNoetherian
  obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ⟩ :=
    MMP.FormalFunctions.nonempty_adicCompletion_pushforwardStalk_linearEquiv_towerLimit_germ
      f F z φ hφ
  exact ⟨bijective_canonicalStalkComparison_of_isProper f z, Φ, hΦ, fun k U hz a s => by
    rw [hΦ, hΦ]
    exact infinitesimalRestrict_smul_res f F z k U hz a s⟩

end MMP

namespace MMP.Foundations.ConeAlgebra

open MMP.Intersection.Scheme

open CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace DirectSum
open MMP.ProjectiveConeSurjection
open Stacks.RelativeProj Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

section

variable (R : Situation.{u})

/-- The degree-one inclusion `R_1 ⟶ R_1` pairwise commutes. -/
private theorem pairwiseCommutes_id :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.PairwiseCommutes (𝟙 (R.algebra.piece 1)) :=
  fun U s t => eq_of_heq (R.mul_comm 1 1 U s t)

/-- The multiplication map `Sym R_1 ⟶ R`. -/
private noncomputable def symHom :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom
      (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)) R.algebra :=
  (Scheme.Modules.isSymmetricAlgebra_symmetricAlgebra R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)).desc _
    (𝟙 _) (pairwiseCommutes_id R)

private theorem symHom_app_gen (U : (TopologicalSpace.Opens R.base)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : (R.algebra.piece 1).val.obj U) :
    ((symHom R).app 1).val.app U
        ((Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)).val.app U x) = x :=
  congrArg (fun f => f.val.app U x)
    ((Scheme.Modules.isSymmetricAlgebra_symmetricAlgebra R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)).desc_extends
      R.algebra (𝟙 _) (pairwiseCommutes_id R))

section Surjective

private instance situationAxioms_sym :
    SituationAxioms (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)) :=
  situationAxioms (symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent R.base (R.algebra.piece 1))

/-- The degree-`n` component of the image of a section under a homomorphism of graded rings of
sections is the image of its degree-`n` component. -/
private theorem gradedSectionHom_apply_component {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {A A' : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra X.ringCatSheaf}
    [SituationAxioms A] [SituationAxioms A'] (φ : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A A')
    (U : X.Opens) (x : (sitOf A).sectionRing U) (n : ℕ) :
    (gradedSectionHom φ U x) n = pieceHom φ n U (x n) := by
  induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, DirectSum.zero_apply, DirectSum.zero_apply, map_zero]
  | of k a =>
    rw [gradedSectionHom_of]
    by_cases h : k = n
    · subst h
      rw [DirectSum.of_eq_same, DirectSum.of_eq_same]
    · erw [DirectSum.of_eq_of_ne k n _ (Ne.symm h), DirectSum.of_eq_of_ne k n _ (Ne.symm h),
        map_zero]
  | add x y hx hy =>
    rw [map_add, DirectSum.add_apply, DirectSum.add_apply, hx, hy, map_add]

/-- In degree zero, `Sym R_1 ⟶ R` is surjective on sections. -/
private theorem surjective_pieceHom_zero (hR : IsConeAlgebra R) (U : R.base.Opens) :
    Function.Surjective (pieceHom (symHom R) 0 U) := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := (hR.bijective_smul_one U).2 y
  refine ⟨c • (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)).one.eval (op U), ?_⟩
  rw [pieceHom_apply]
  erw [((((symHom R).app ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.app (op U)).hom.map_smul c _)]
  erw [(symHom R).map_one (op U)]

/-- In degree one, `Sym R_1 ⟶ R` is surjective on sections. -/
private theorem surjective_pieceHom_one (U : R.base.Opens) :
    Function.Surjective (pieceHom (symHom R) 1 U) := by
  intro y
  refine ⟨(Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)).val.app (op U) y, ?_⟩
  rw [pieceHom_apply]
  exact symHom_app_gen R (op U) y

/-- Over an affine open, `Sym R_1 ⟶ R` is surjective on sections in every degree, because
`Γ(U, R)` is generated by its degree-one part over its degree-zero part. -/
private theorem surjective_pieceHom (hR : IsConeAlgebra R) {U : R.base.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (pieceHom (symHom R) n U) := by
  set ψ := symHom R
  have hrange : ∀ w ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(R.sectionRingGrading U 0)
      (R.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (R.sectionRing U)),
      w ∈ (gradedSectionHom ψ U).toRingHom.range := by
    intro w hw
    induction hw using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hx
      obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := surjective_pieceHom_one R U a
      exact ⟨DirectSum.of _ 1 b, (gradedSectionHom_of ψ U 1 b).trans (congrArg _ hb)⟩
    | algebraMap r =>
      obtain ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩⟩ := r
      obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := surjective_pieceHom_zero R hR U a
      exact ⟨DirectSum.of _ 0 b, (gradedSectionHom_of ψ U 0 b).trans (congrArg _ hb)⟩
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => exact add_mem hx hy
    | mul x y _ _ hx hy => exact mul_mem hx hy
  intro y
  have hy : DirectSum.of _ n y ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(R.sectionRingGrading U 0)
      (R.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (R.sectionRing U)) := by
    rw [adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top R U hU (hR.isLocallyDegreeOneGenerated U)]
    trivial
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hrange _ hy
  refine ⟨x n, ?_⟩
  have h := congrArg (fun w : R.sectionRing U => w n) hx
  simp only at h
  erw [gradedSectionHom_apply_component, DirectSum.of_eq_same] at h
  exact h

/-- `Sym R_1 ⟶ R` is an epimorphism in every degree. -/
private theorem epi_symHom_app (hR : IsConeAlgebra R) (n : ℤ) : Epi ((symHom R).app n) := by
  rcases lt_or_ge n 0 with hn | hn
  · exact (R.negative_isZero n hn).epi _
  · obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Int.eq_ofNat_of_zero_le hn
    exact Scheme.epi_of_surjective_of_isAffineOpen _ fun U hU => surjective_pieceHom R hR hU m

end Surjective

/-- `Proj_Y R` is a closed subscheme of the projective bundle `𝐏(R_1)`, over `Y`; so its
projection is projective. -/
private theorem isProjective_relativeProjToBase (hR : IsConeAlgebra R)
    [IsLocallyNoetherian R.base] :
    IsProjective R.relativeProjToBase := by
  haveI := hR.isCoherent_one
  let ι := ProjectiveConeSurjection.inducedMap
    (A := Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra R.base (R.algebra.piece 1)) (B := R.algebra)
    (symHom R) (epi_symHom_app R hR)
  have h2 : IsClosedImmersion
      (Stacks.RelativeProj.bundlePresentationIso (R.algebra.piece 1)).symm.hom := inferInstance
  refine @isProjective_of_isClosedImmersion _ _ (R.algebra.piece 1) _ _ _
    (@IsClosedImmersion.comp _ _ _ ι _
      (ProjectiveConeSurjection.isClosedImmersion_inducedMap _ _) h2)
    _ ?_
  refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans ((congrArg (ι ≫ ·)
    (Stacks.RelativeProj.bundlePresentationIso_inv_comp_toBase (R.algebra.piece 1))).trans ?_)
  exact ProjectiveConeSurjection.inducedMap_comp_relativeProjToBase _ _

/-- On a quasi-compact `Proj` of a graded ring generated in degree one over its degree-zero part,
the twisting sheaf `𝒪(1)` is ample. -/
private theorem isAmple_twistingSheaf_one_of_adjoin {S σ : Type u} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S]
    [AddSubgroupClass σ S] (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (𝒮 1 : Set S) = ⊤) [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)] :
    letI := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistMapsInvertible.isInvertibleModule_twistingSheaf_of_adjoin
      𝒮 hgen 1
    Stacks.Ample.IsAmple (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf 𝒮 1) := by
  letI := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistMapsInvertible.isInvertibleModule_twistingSheaf_of_adjoin
    𝒮 hgen 1
  refine (Stacks.AmpleBridge.isAmple_iff_isAmple _ _).mpr
    (Stacks.ProjDegreeOneCover.isAmple_twistingModule_one _ inferInstance fun x => ?_)
  exact ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.exists_mem_degreeOne_notMem _ hgen
    (p := x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal) x.not_irrelevant_le

/-- `𝒪_Z(1)` is ample over every affine open of `Y`. -/
private theorem isRelativelyAmple_twistSheaf_one (hR : IsConeAlgebra R)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule R.relativeProj (R.twistSheaf 1)] :
    Stacks.RelativeAmple.IsRelativelyAmple R.relativeProjToBase (R.twistSheaf 1) := by
  haveI := hR.isProper_relativeProjToBase
  refine ⟨inferInstance, fun V hV => ?_⟩
  set W : R.base.affineOpens := ⟨V, hV⟩
  set c := R.relativeProjChart W with hc
  have hrange : Set.range c.base = Set.range (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι.base := by
    rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι, hc]
    exact congrArg (fun U : R.relativeProj.Opens => (U : Set R.relativeProj))
      (opensRange_relativeProjChart R W)
  set φ := IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq c (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι hrange
  have hfac : φ.hom ≫ (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι = c :=
    IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq_hom_fac c (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι hrange
  have hfac' : φ.inv ≫ c = (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι := (Iso.inv_comp_eq φ).mpr hfac.symm
  have hgen := Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top R W.1
    W.2 (hR.isLocallyDegreeOneGenerated W.1)
  haveI : CompactSpace (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V) :=
    isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp
      (QuasiCompact.isCompact_preimage (f := R.relativeProjToBase) _ V.isOpen hV.isCompact)
  have hcpt : CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (R.sectionRingGrading W.1)) :=
    (Scheme.homeoOfIso φ).symm.compactSpace
  haveI hinvC : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (R.sectionRingGrading W.1))
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) 1) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistMapsInvertible.isInvertibleModule_twistingSheaf_of_adjoin _
      hgen 1
  haveI hinvP : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback φ.inv).obj
        (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) 1)) :=
    Stacks.RingedSpace.algebraicGeometryIsInvertible_modulePullback φ.inv.toLRSHom.toShHom _
  haveI hinvQ : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι).obj (R.twistSheaf 1)) :=
    Stacks.RingedSpace.algebraicGeometryIsInvertible_modulePullback
      (R.relativeProjToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι.toLRSHom.toShHom _
  have hamp : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (R.sectionRingGrading W.1))
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) 1) :=
    isAmple_twistingSheaf_one_of_adjoin _ hgen
  have hA := Stacks.AmplePullback.isAmple_modulePullback_of_isClosedImmersion φ.inv
    (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) 1) hamp
  have e₁ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback c).obj (R.twistSheaf 1) ≅
      ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) 1 :=
    ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback c).app (R.twistSheaf 1)).symm ≪≫
      R.twistSheafChartIso 1 W
  have e := (Scheme.Modules.pullback φ.inv).mapIso e₁.symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp φ.inv c).app (R.twistSheaf 1) ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr hfac').app (R.twistSheaf 1)
  exact (Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.isAmple_congr _ _ e).mp hA

/-- **Stacks 0AG7 for the regular module.** On `Proj` of a graded ring with Noetherian degree-zero
part, generated over it by finitely many elements of degree one, the canonical map
`𝒮 m → Γ(Proj 𝒮, 𝒪(m))` is bijective for all large `m`. -/
private theorem exists_bijective_degreeSection {S σ : Type u} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S]
    [AddSubgroupClass σ S] (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮] [IsNoetherianRing (𝒮 0)] {r : ℕ}
    (fam : Fin r → S) (hfam : ∀ i, fam i ∈ 𝒮 1)
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range fam) = ⊤) :
    ∃ m₀ : ℕ, ∀ m ≥ m₀, Function.Bijective (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection 𝒮 m) := by
  open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections in
  obtain ⟨n₀, hn₀⟩ := exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections_of_finite
      𝒮 (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮) fam hfam hgen
  refine ⟨n₀.toNat, fun m hm => ?_⟩
  let e : 𝒮 m → ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading (S := S) 𝒮 (m : ℤ) := fun b =>
    ⟨b, by simpa [ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading] using b.2⟩
  have he : Function.Bijective e :=
    ⟨fun a b h => Subtype.ext (congrArg Subtype.val h), fun c =>
      ⟨⟨c, by simpa [ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading] using c.2⟩, rfl⟩⟩
  exact (hn₀ m (by omega)).comp he

/-- Over an affine open `W` of a locally Noetherian `Y`, the canonical map
`Γ(W, R_m) → Γ(Proj Γ(W, R), 𝒪(m))` is bijective for all large `m`. -/
private theorem exists_bijective_degreeSection_sectionRing (hR : IsConeAlgebra R)
    [IsLocallyNoetherian R.base] (W : R.base.affineOpens) :
    ∃ m₀ : ℕ, ∀ m ≥ m₀, Function.Bijective
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m) := by
  classical
  haveI := hR.isCoherent_one
  haveI : IsNoetherianRing Γ(R.base, W.1) :=
    IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian (X := R.base) ⟨W.1, W.2⟩
  haveI := R.isIso_sectionRingZeroMap W.1 (hR.bijective_smul_one W.1)
  haveI : IsNoetherianRing (R.sectionRingGrading W.1 0) :=
    isNoetherianRing_of_ringEquiv _
      (asIso (R.sectionRingZeroMap W.1)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := (finite_sections_of_isAffineOpen (R.algebra.piece 1) W.1 W.2).fg_top
  let fam : Fin g.card → R.sectionRing W.1 := fun i =>
    DirectSum.of (R.sectionPieces W.1) 1 (g.equivFin.symm i).1
  refine exists_bijective_degreeSection _ fam (fun i => ⟨_, rfl⟩) (top_unique ?_)
  rw [← adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top R W.1 W.2
    (hR.isLocallyDegreeOneGenerated W.1)]
  refine Algebra.adjoin_le ((sectionRingGrading_one_le_adjoin R W.1 g hg).trans
    (Algebra.adjoin_mono ?_))
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨g.equivFin ⟨x, hx⟩, by simp [fam]⟩

/-- The homogeneous element of `Γ(W, R)` of degree `m` attached to a section of `R_m` over `W`. -/
private abbrev homElem (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) : R.sectionRingGrading W.1 m :=
  ⟨DirectSum.of (R.sectionPieces W.1) m a, AddMonoidHom.mem_range.mpr ⟨a, rfl⟩⟩

/-- A morphism `R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪_Z(m)` reads, on the chart over every affine open `W` of `Y`, as the
canonical map `Γ(W, R_m) → Γ(Proj Γ(W, R), 𝒪(m))`. -/
private def IsDegreeSectionOnCharts (m : ℕ) (ψ : R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj (R.twistSheaf m)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (W : R.base.affineOpens) (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)),
    (R.twistSheafChartIso m W).hom.val.app (op ⊤)
        ((R.twistSheaf m).val.map
          (homOfLE ((Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange _).trans
            (opensRange_relativeProjChart R W)).le).op
          (ψ.val.app (op W.1) a)) =
      ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m
        (homElem R m W a)

/-- The section `a / 1` of `𝒪(m)` on the chart `Proj Γ(W, R)`, restricted to the part of the chart
lying over `W`. -/
private noncomputable def chartSec (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    ToType ((twistChart R m W).val.obj
      (op (relativeProjChart R W ⁻¹ᵁ (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W.1)))) :=
  (twistChart R m W).val.map (homOfLE le_top).op
    (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m
      (homElem R m W a))

private theorem degreeSection_homElem_add (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a b : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m
        (homElem R m W (a + b)) =
      ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m
          (homElem R m W a) +
        ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m
          (homElem R m W b) := by
  have helem : homElem R m W (a + b) = homElem R m W a + homElem R m W b :=
    Subtype.ext (map_add (DirectSum.of (R.sectionPieces W.1) m) a b)
  rw [helem]
  exact map_add (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSectionHom
    (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m) _ _

private theorem chartSec_add (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a b : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    chartSec R m W (a + b) = chartSec R m W a + chartSec R m W b :=
  (congrArg (fun z => (twistChart R m W).val.map (homOfLE le_top).op z)
    (degreeSection_homElem_add R m W a b)).trans
    (map_add ((twistChart R m W).val.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom _ _)

private theorem chartSec_smul (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (r : R.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W.1))
    (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    chartSec R m W (r • a) = chartBaseFunction W r • chartSec R m W a := by
  have hfun : chartBaseFunction W r =
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (R.sectionRingGrading W.1)).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE le_top).op
        (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShiftedSections.degreeZeroPullbackHom
          (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) (sectionRingZeroMap R W.1 r)) := by
    have h := congrArg (fun k => k r)
      (relativeProjToBase_app_relativeProjChart_app R W)
    simp only [CommRingCat.comp_apply] at h
    exact h
  have hr : ((sectionRingZeroMap R W.1 r : R.sectionRingGrading W.1 0) :
      R.sectionRing W.1) = R.sectionRingBaseMap W.1 r :=
    congrArg Subtype.val
      (GradedRing.projZeroRingHom'_apply_coe _
        ⟨_, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero R W.1 r⟩)
  have hsec :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroToGlobalSections_pullbackDegreeZero
    (R.sectionRingGrading W.1)
    (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistGrading (S := R.sectionRing W.1)
      (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) (m : ℤ))
    (sectionRingZeroMap R W.1 r)
    ⟨(homElem R m W a).1, by simpa [ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistGrading,
      ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading, ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.homogeneousSubmodule]
        using (homElem R m W a).2⟩
    ⟨(homElem R m W (r • a)).1, by simpa [ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistGrading,
      ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.integerGrading, ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.homogeneousSubmodule]
        using (homElem R m W (r • a)).2⟩
    (by
      change DirectSum.of (R.sectionPieces W.1) m (r • a) =
        ((sectionRingZeroMap R W.1 r : R.sectionRingGrading W.1 0) :
          R.sectionRing W.1) * DirectSum.of (R.sectionPieces W.1) m a
      rw [hr]
      exact (sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of R W.1 m r a).symm)
  refine (congrArg (fun z => (twistChart R m W).val.map (homOfLE le_top).op z)
    hsec).trans ?_
  refine (PresheafOfModules.map_smul (twistChart R m W).val
    (homOfLE le_top).op _ _).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (fun t => t • chartSec R m W a) hfun.symm

/-- The section `a / 1` of `𝒪_Z(m)` over the part of `Z` lying over `W`: the section `a / 1` of
the chart twist, read in the glued twisting sheaf. -/
private noncomputable def twistSec (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    ToType ((twistSheaf R m).val.obj
      (op (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W.1))) :=
  (twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W
    (preimage_le_opensRange_relativeProjChart W)).inv.hom (chartSec R m W a)

private theorem twistSec_add (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a b : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    twistSec R m W (a + b) = twistSec R m W a + twistSec R m W b :=
  (congrArg (twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W
    (preimage_le_opensRange_relativeProjChart W)).inv.hom (chartSec_add R m W a b)).trans
    (map_add _ _ _)

private theorem twistSec_smul (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (r : R.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W.1))
    (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    twistSec R m W (r • a) = baseFunction W r • twistSec R m W a := by
  unfold twistSec
  rw [chartSec_smul]
  exact (twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W
    (preimage_le_opensRange_relativeProjChart W)).inv.hom.map_smul (baseFunction W r)
      (chartSec R m W a)

/-- The sections of `g_* 𝒪_Z(m)` over an affine open `W` of `Y`, as a module over `Γ(W, 𝒪_Y)`. -/
private noncomputable def twistPushSections (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens) :
    ModuleCat (R.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W.1)) :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjToBase R)).obj
    (twistSheaf R m)).val.obj (op W.1)

/-- The map `Γ(W, R_m) ⟶ Γ(W, g_* 𝒪_Z(m))`, `a ↦ a / 1`. -/
private noncomputable def twistSecHom (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens) :
    (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1) ⟶ twistPushSections R m W :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom (X := (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1))
    (Y := twistPushSections R m W)
    { toFun := twistSec R m W
      map_add' := twistSec_add R m W
      map_smul' := twistSec_smul R m W }

/-- Comparing the section `a / 1` on the chart over `W` down to the chart over `W' ≤ W` gives the
section `a|_{W'} / 1`. -/
private theorem twistPushforwardMap_map_chartSec (m : ℕ) {W W' : R.base.affineOpens}
    (h : W'.1 ≤ W.1) (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    ((twistPushforwardMap R m (show W' ≤ W from h)).val.app
        (op (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W'.1))).hom
        (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjChart R W)).obj
          (twistChart R m W)).val.map
          (homOfLE ((relativeProjToBase R).preimage_mono h)).op
          (chartSec R m W a)) =
      chartSec R m W' ((R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op a) := by
  refine Subtype.ext (funext fun y => ?_)
  refine (twistPushforwardMap_val R m (show W' ≤ W from h) _ y).trans ?_
  change Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.fibreMap _ _ y.1
      ((ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection _ m (homElem R m W a)).1 ⟨_, trivial⟩) =
    (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection _ m (homElem R m W' _)).1 ⟨y.1, trivial⟩
  refine (congrArg (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.fibreMap _ _ y.1)
    (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection_val _ m (homElem R m W a) ⟨_, trivial⟩)).trans ?_
  refine (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.fibreMap_mk _ _ y.1 _ 1).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection_val _ m
    (homElem R m W' ((R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op a))
    ⟨y.1, trivial⟩).symm
  refine (congrArg (fun t => LocalizedModule.mk _ t) (a₂ := 1)
    (Subtype.ext (map_one (gradedSectionRestriction R W'.1 W.1 h).toRingHom))).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (fun x => LocalizedModule.mk x 1)
    (gradedSectionRestriction_of R W'.1 W.1 h m a)

/-- The sections `a / 1` commute with restriction between affine opens of `Y`. -/
private theorem twistSec_restrict (m : ℕ) {W W' : R.base.affineOpens}
    (h : W'.1 ≤ W.1) (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    twistSec R m W' ((R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op a) =
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjToBase R)).obj
        (twistSheaf R m)).val.map (homOfLE h).op (twistSec R m W a) := by
  have hV' := preimage_le_opensRange_relativeProjChart (s := R) W'
  have hV := preimage_le_opensRange_relativeProjChart (s := R) W
  have hle : relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W'.1 ≤
      relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W.1 :=
    (relativeProjToBase R).preimage_mono h
  set e' := twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W' hV'
  set e := twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W hV
  set b := (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op a
  set z := ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjToBase R)).obj
    (twistSheaf R m)).val.map (homOfLE h).op (twistSec R m W a)
  have hinv : e.hom.hom (twistSec R m W a) = chartSec R m W a :=
    congrArg (fun k => k.hom (chartSec R m W a)) e.inv_hom_id
  have key : e'.hom.hom z = chartSec R m W' b := by
    refine (twistPushforwardMap_twistSectionsIso R m (show W' ≤ W from h) hV'
      z).symm.trans ?_
    have hres := twistSectionsIso_restrict (twistTransition R m) W hV hle
      (twistSec R m W a)
    refine (congrArg (fun t => ((twistPushforwardMap R m (show W' ≤ W from h)).val.app
      (op (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W'.1))).hom t) hres).trans ?_
    refine (congrArg (fun t => ((twistPushforwardMap R m (show W' ≤ W from h)).val.app
      (op (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W'.1))).hom
        (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjChart R W)).obj
          (twistChart R m W)).val.restrictₛₗ (homOfLE hle).op t)) hinv).trans ?_
    exact twistPushforwardMap_map_chartSec R m h a
  have hinv' : e'.hom.hom (twistSec R m W' b) = chartSec R m W' b :=
    congrArg (fun k => k.hom (chartSec R m W' b)) e'.inv_hom_id
  have h1 : e'.inv.hom (e'.hom.hom (twistSec R m W' b)) = twistSec R m W' b :=
    congrArg (fun k => k.hom (twistSec R m W' b)) e'.hom_inv_id
  have h2 : e'.inv.hom (e'.hom.hom z) = z := congrArg (fun k => k.hom z) e'.hom_inv_id
  exact h1.symm.trans ((congrArg e'.inv.hom (hinv'.trans key.symm)).trans h2)

/-- Restriction of sections of a sheaf of modules along an equality of opens is bijective. -/
private theorem bijective_map_homOfLE_of_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) {A B : X.Opens}
    (h : A = B) :
    Function.Bijective (fun x : M.val.obj (op B) => M.val.map (homOfLE h.le).op x) := by
  subst h
  have hid : ∀ x : M.val.obj (op A), M.val.map (homOfLE (le_refl A)).op x = x := fun x => by
    rw [show (homOfLE (le_refl A)).op = 𝟙 (op A) from Subsingleton.elim _ _,
      PresheafOfModules.map_id]
    rfl
  exact ⟨fun x y hxy => (hid x).symm.trans (hxy.trans (hid y)), fun y => ⟨y, hid y⟩⟩

/-- **The canonical map `R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪_Z(m)`.** On the sections over an affine open `W` it is
`a ↦ a / 1`, read on the chart `Proj Γ(W, R)`; these local maps are linear over `Γ(W, 𝒪_Y)` and
commute with restriction between affine opens, so they extend from the basis of affine opens. -/
private noncomputable def pieceToPushforward (m : ℕ) : R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj (R.twistSheaf m) :=
  Stacks.BasisRestriction.moduleSheafHomOfSectionHomOnBasis (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ))
    ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjToBase R)).obj
      (twistSheaf R m))
    (fun W : R.base.affineOpens => W.1) (fun W => twistSecHom R m W)
    (isBasis_range_affineOpens (s := R)) (fun _ _ h a => twistSec_restrict R m h a)

private theorem pieceToPushforward_app (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)) :
    ((pieceToPushforward R m).val.app (op W.1)).hom a = twistSec R m W a :=
  congrArg (fun k => k.hom a)
    (Stacks.BasisRestriction.moduleSheafHomOfSectionHomOnBasis_app
      (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ))
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (relativeProjToBase R)).obj
        (twistSheaf R m))
      (fun W : R.base.affineOpens => W.1) (fun W => twistSecHom R m W)
      (isBasis_range_affineOpens (s := R)) (fun _ _ h a => twistSec_restrict R m h a) W)

/-- Two successive restrictions of a section, in the presheaf of abelian groups, are one. -/
private theorem presheaf_map_map {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) {A B C : X.Opensᵒᵖ}
    (f : C ⟶ B) (g : B ⟶ A) (h : C ⟶ A) (x : ToType (M.presheaf.obj C)) :
    M.presheaf.map g (M.presheaf.map f x) = M.presheaf.map h x := by
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  exact congrArg (fun k => M.presheaf.map k x) (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

private theorem isDegreeSectionOnCharts_pieceToPushforward (m : ℕ) :
    IsDegreeSectionOnCharts R m (pieceToPushforward R m) := by
  intro W a
  have hV := preimage_le_opensRange_relativeProjChart (s := R) W
  have hA : relativeProjChart R W ⁻¹ᵁ (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W.1) = ⊤ :=
    top_unique fun x _ => (opensRange_relativeProjChart R W).le ⟨x, rfl⟩
  refine (bijective_map_homOfLE_of_eq (twistChart R (m : ℤ) W) hA).1 ?_
  change _ = chartSec R m W a
  have hE := (Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange (R.relativeProjChart W)).trans
    (opensRange_relativeProjChart R W)
  have hnat := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    (twistSheafChartIso R (m : ℤ) W).hom.val (homOfLE hA.le).op
    ((twistSheaf R m).val.map (homOfLE hE.le).op (twistSec R m W a))
  have hres :
      ((twistSheaf R m).restrict (relativeProjChart R W)).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE hA.le).op
        ((twistSheaf R m).presheaf.map (homOfLE hE.le).op (twistSec R m W a)) =
      (twistSheaf R m).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE ((relativeProjChart R W).image_preimage_le
          (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W.1))).op (twistSec R m W a) := by
    rw [Scheme.Modules.restrict_map]
    exact presheaf_map_map (twistSheaf R m) _ _ _ _
  have h4 := twistSheafChartIso_hom_map_homOfLE R m W hV (twistSec R m W a)
  have h5 : (twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W hV).hom.hom
      (twistSec R m W a) = chartSec R m W a :=
    congrArg (fun k => k.hom (chartSec R m W a))
      (twistSectionsIso (twistTransition R m) W hV).inv_hom_id
  refine (congrArg (fun z => (twistChart R (m : ℤ) W).val.map (homOfLE hA.le).op
    ((twistSheafChartIso R (m : ℤ) W).hom.val.app (op ⊤)
      ((twistSheaf R m).val.map (homOfLE hE.le).op z))) (pieceToPushforward_app R m W a)).trans ?_
  refine hnat.symm.trans ?_
  refine (congrArg (fun z => ((twistSheafChartIso R (m : ℤ) W).hom.val.app
    (op (relativeProjChart R W ⁻¹ᵁ (relativeProjToBase R ⁻¹ᵁ W.1)))).hom z)
    hres).trans ?_
  exact h4.trans h5

/-- **A morphism `R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪_Z(m)` bijective on the sections over each member of an affine open
cover is an isomorphism**: both sheaves are quasi-coherent (`g` is quasi-compact and
quasi-separated), and a morphism of quasi-coherent modules on an affine scheme is an isomorphism as
soon as it is bijective on global sections. -/
private theorem isIso_of_bijective_app_affineCover (hR : IsConeAlgebra R) {m : ℕ}
    (ψ : R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj (R.twistSheaf m))
    (s : Finset R.base.affineOpens) (hs : ∀ y : R.base, ∃ W ∈ s, y ∈ W.1)
    (h : ∀ W ∈ s, Function.Bijective (fun a => ψ.val.app (op W.1) a)) : IsIso ψ := by
  haveI hP := hR.isProper_relativeProjToBase
  haveI := hR.isInvertibleModule_twistSheaf (m : ℤ)
  haveI : UniversallyClosed R.relativeProjToBase := hP.toUniversallyClosed
  haveI : IsSeparated R.relativeProjToBase := hP.toIsSeparated
  -- given explicitly: instance search for these times out
  haveI : QuasiCompact R.relativeProjToBase :=
    instQuasiCompactOfUniversallyClosed R.relativeProjToBase
  haveI : QuasiSeparated R.relativeProjToBase :=
    IsSeparated.instQuasiSeparated R.relativeProjToBase
  haveI : (R.twistSheaf (m : ℤ)).IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule (R.twistSheaf (m : ℤ))
  haveI : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj
      (R.twistSheaf m)).IsQuasicoherent :=
    ProperCoherentFiniteType.isQuasicoherent_pushforward R.relativeProjToBase
      (R.twistSheaf (m : ℤ)) inferInstance
  haveI : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).IsQuasicoherent := R.isQuasicoherent (m : ℤ)
  refine Stacks.Coherent.isIso_of_bijective_app_of_affineCover (X := R.base)
    (fun W : s => (W.1 : R.base.affineOpens)) ?_ ψ (fun W => h W.1 W.2)
  refine top_unique fun y _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hy⟩ := hs y
  exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hy⟩

/-- A morphism which is the canonical map on the charts is bijective on the sections over an
affine open on whose chart the canonical map is bijective. -/
private theorem bijective_app_of_isDegreeSectionOnCharts {m : ℕ}
    {ψ : R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj (R.twistSheaf m)}
    (hψ : IsDegreeSectionOnCharts R m ψ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
    (hb : Function.Bijective
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m)) :
    Function.Bijective (fun a => ψ.val.app (op W.1) a) := by
  set e := R.twistSheafChartIso m W
  have hE := (Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange (R.relativeProjChart W)).trans
    (opensRange_relativeProjChart R W)
  have hiso : Function.Bijective (fun x => e.hom.val.app (op ⊤) x) := by
    refine Function.bijective_iff_has_inverse.mpr ⟨fun y => e.inv.val.app (op ⊤) y, fun x => ?_,
      fun y => ?_⟩
    · exact congrArg (fun f => f.val.app (op ⊤) x) e.hom_inv_id
    · exact congrArg (fun f => f.val.app (op ⊤) y) e.inv_hom_id
  have hΨ := hiso.comp (bijective_map_homOfLE_of_eq (R.twistSheaf m) hE)
  have hι : Function.Bijective (homElem R m W) := by
    refine ⟨fun a b hab => DirectSum.of_injective (β := R.sectionPieces W.1) m
      (congrArg Subtype.val hab), fun x => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := AddMonoidHom.mem_range.mp x.2
    exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩
  refine (Function.Bijective.of_comp_iff' hΨ (fun a => ψ.val.app (op W.1) a)).mp ?_
  exact (congrArg Function.Bijective (funext (hψ W))).mpr (hb.comp hι)

/-- The canonical map `R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪_Z(m)`, pinned chartwise, is an isomorphism for `m ≫ 0`. -/
private theorem exists_pieceToPushforwardTwist (hR : IsConeAlgebra R) [IsNoetherian R.base] :
    ∃ φ : ∀ m : ℕ, R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj (R.twistSheaf m),
        (∀ m : ℕ, IsDegreeSectionOnCharts R m (φ m)) ∧
        ∃ m₀ : ℕ, ∀ m ≥ m₀, IsIso (φ m) := by
  classical
  refine ⟨pieceToPushforward R, isDegreeSectionOnCharts_pieceToPushforward R, ?_⟩
  have hY : CompactSpace R.base := ‹IsNoetherian R.base›.toCompactSpace
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (@isCompact_univ _ _ hY).elim_finite_subcover
    (fun W : R.base.affineOpens => ((W.1 : Set R.base) : Set R.base))
    (fun W => W.1.isOpen)
    (fun y _ => by
      obtain ⟨W, hW, hyW, -⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (X := R.base) (x := y)
        (U := ⊤) trivial
      exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hyW⟩)
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian R.base := IsNoetherian.toIsLocallyNoetherian
  have hbd := fun W : R.base.affineOpens =>
    exists_bijective_degreeSection_sectionRing R hR W
  refine ⟨s.sup fun W => (hbd W).choose, fun m hm => ?_⟩
  refine isIso_of_bijective_app_affineCover R hR (pieceToPushforward R m) s (fun y => ?_)
    fun W hW => bijective_app_of_isDegreeSectionOnCharts R
      (isDegreeSectionOnCharts_pieceToPushforward R m) W
      ((hbd W).choose_spec m ((Finset.le_sup hW).trans hm))
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hyW⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hs (Set.mem_univ y))
  exact ⟨W, hW, hyW⟩

end

/-- Let `Y` be Noetherian and `R` a graded `𝒪_Y`-algebra generated in degree one, with
`R_0 = 𝒪_Y`, every `R_m` coherent, and `R` a sheaf of domains. Let `g : Proj_Y R ⟶ Y` be the
projection. Then `g` is projective, and `𝒪(1)` is invertible and `g`-ample. Moreover there is a
map `φ_m : R_m ⟶ g_* 𝒪(m)` for every `m`, sending a section `a` over an affine open `W` to the
section `a/1` of `𝒪(m)` on the chart `Proj Γ(W, R)`, and `φ_m` is an isomorphism for every
`m ≫ 0`. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_foundation_degree_one_relative_proj_high_sections"]
public theorem isProjective_and_isIso_pieceToPushforwardTwist (R : Situation.{u})
    [IsNoetherian R.base] (hR : IsConeAlgebra R)
    (hcoh : ∀ n : ℕ, Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent (R.algebra.piece n))
    (hdom : ∀ U : R.base.Opens, Nonempty U → IsDomain (R.sectionRing U)) :
    IsProjective R.relativeProjToBase ∧
      (∃ _ : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule R.relativeProj (R.twistSheaf 1),
        Stacks.RelativeAmple.IsRelativelyAmple R.relativeProjToBase (R.twistSheaf 1)) ∧
      ∃ φ : ∀ m : ℕ, R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward R.relativeProjToBase).obj (R.twistSheaf m),
        (∀ (m : ℕ) (W : R.base.affineOpens)
            (a : (R.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W.1)),
          (R.twistSheafChartIso m W).hom.val.app (op ⊤)
              ((R.twistSheaf m).val.map
                (homOfLE ((Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange _).trans
                  (opensRange_relativeProjChart R W)).le).op
                ((φ m).val.app (op W.1) a)) =
            ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection (R.sectionRingGrading W.1) m
              ⟨DirectSum.of (R.sectionPieces W.1) m a,
                AddMonoidHom.mem_range.mpr ⟨a, rfl⟩⟩) ∧
        ∃ m₀ : ℕ, ∀ m ≥ m₀, IsIso (φ m) := by
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian R.base := IsNoetherian.toIsLocallyNoetherian
  haveI := hR.isInvertibleModule_twistSheaf 1
  exact ⟨isProjective_relativeProjToBase R hR, ⟨inferInstance,
    isRelativelyAmple_twistSheaf_one R hR⟩, exists_pieceToPushforwardTwist R hR⟩

end MMP.Foundations.ConeAlgebra
